      "content": "\"strategic stalemate\" is an interesting way to put it. but honestly, looking at the chaos and the power vacuum that followed, doesn't it seem more like a fundamental failure of liberal interventionism? like, if the goal was stability in the region, it clearly didn't work. why wouldn't it be classified as a failure?",
